# === Signing keys and their passwords — NEVER committed (docs D-010) ===
# The release key of Read Files Tech lives OUTSIDE this repository. The Flutter clone keeps it under
# android/, ignored only by android/.gitignore: a merge that removes android/ removes that file too,
# and the key becomes committable there. This root file ignores every form of it from the first
# commit, whatever directory it lands in.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.der
key.properties
keystore.properties
# Their copies: a backup of the key is the key (security review of the skeleton, 2026-10-10, G1).
*.jks.*
*.keystore.*
key.properties.*
keystore.properties.*
*.properties.bak
.env
.env.*

# === Android local config ===
local.properties

# === Gradle ===
.gradle/
build/
**/build/

# === Kotlin 2.x compiler session and error files ===
.kotlin/

# === IDE ===
.idea/
*.iml
.project
.classpath
.settings/

# === Android Studio / native ===
captures/
.cxx/
*.ap_
*.dex
*.class
obj/

# === OS ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local Claude Code agent worktrees (nested git checkouts), never part of the repository
/.claude/worktrees/

# Python bytecode of the tools (tools/corpus imports its generators)
__pycache__/
